.TH "PB-CONFIG-CUSTOMIZE-IMPORT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-customize-import - Validate and replace local preferences from a JSON file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config customize import <file> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate and replace local preferences from a JSON file

.PP
Validate the JSON preferences document, then replace local customization with its contents. A failed validation leaves the current preferences in place.

.PP
Customization is local to this CLI installation. It can change shortcuts, command defaults, and terminal appearance without changing account credentials or remote resources. Validate or explain preferences before applying an unfamiliar document.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for import

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-customize(1)\fP
